<title>INDIA: India soybean prices steady in limited activity.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices steady in limited activity.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in limited trading activity on Wednesday, dealers said, with arrivals in markets very low.</p>
<p>Most markets were closed and there were no arrivals in several markets, dealers said. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell sharply on increased selling against poor demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 500 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 400 rupees per tonne today. The undertone was down.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were steady and trading activity was at the lowest level. Soymeal yellow was $300-302 September-October shipment for current season.  Soymeal yellow was $280-282 per tonne November, December and January shipment. Rapeseed extraction was $130-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550 rupees per tonne FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
